    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d384-a2">

                <pb facs="0718" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg658"/>

                <head>Mr. Washburn to Señor
                        Berges.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Asuncion</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-02-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 22, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The present critical condition of affairs
                    in and near this capital has rendered it necessary for me to take into my
                    service several persons in addition to those hitherto connected with this
                    legation.</p>
                <p>The following is a list of those employed by me:</p>
                <p>Carlos Meincke, German, private secretary; Porter C. Bliss, American; James
                    Man-love, American; George Hamilton, English; Catherm Leahy, English; Anabella
                    Casal, Paraguayan; Basilio Jarra, Paraguayan; Melchora Jarra, Paraguayan.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion to tender to your excellency assurances of
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES A. WASHBURN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">JosÉ Berges</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister for Foreign Relations.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
